I'll add this.

At first I was convinced that this is a good idea. After thinking about it for a while I'm not sure anymore:

If from and to are the same, then we have one big ambiguity: The axis we get from `Quat::from_rotation_arc(foo,bar).to_axis_angle()` is not well defined anymore and could be anything, which is bad as the arc would point to a random direction.

On the other hand we have:

- in the short case, the angle is 0.0 so nothing gets rendered anyways
- in the long case, I just modified the closure a bit to
  ```rust
        self.arc_from_to(center, from, to, |angle| {
            if angle > 0.0 {
                TAU - angle
            } else if angle < 0.0 {
                -TAU - angle
            } else {
                0.0
            }
        })
  ```
  which means we will also get the 0.0 angle in this case and nothing gets rendered

So in the end the orientation ambiguity doesn't really matter anymore. I tested and confirmed that this is indeed the case.
